<div class="text-center">
    <h1 class="display-4">External ID and Verified ID</h1>
    <p>This sample shows how an application combines customer sign-in, digital credentials,
        and identity verification. Microsoft Entra External ID signs the user in;
        Microsoft Entra Verified ID handles credential issuance and presentation after sign-in.</p>
</div>
<h2>What you can try</h2>
<ol>
    <li><strong>Sign up or sign in</strong> using the normal hosted External ID experience.</li>
    <li><strong>Issue a loyalty credential</strong> from your account details and add it to Microsoft Authenticator.</li>
    <li><strong>Select and verify a configured credential</strong> using the Verified ID Request Service.
        The default is the loyalty card; other credentials need account-binding and profile claim mappings.</li>
    <li><strong>Try identity verification (IDV)</strong> with the TrueIdentity demo provider,
        which issues a separate credential after its proofing experience. Present that credential
        to the application to complete the staged demo.</li>
</ol>
<p>A validated TrueIdentity presentation completes verification without changing
    the signed-in account's profile. Returning from the provider alone is not proof of success.</p>
<p>This is an educational demo. The IDV provider and public callback endpoints must be configured;
    production use requires stronger binding between the proofed identity and the signed-in account.</p>
<h2>Setup and integration guidance</h2>
<ul>
    <li><a href="https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/entra/external-id/customers/verified-id-setup-issuance-presentation">Set up Microsoft Entra Verified ID</a>
        in an External ID tenant for credential issuance and presentation.</li>
    <li><a href="https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/entra/external-id/customers/identity-verification-integration">Identity verification integration for Microsoft Entra External ID</a>
        explains the IDV integration patterns. This sample uses the credential-based presentation pattern.</li>
</ul>
